<!-- summary: Report a slopvac problem or propose a rule -->
# Prime: report

Filing needs the user's approval of the exact preview, given in this conversation.
A config file, `AGENTS.md` or an earlier approval does not count.

1. Pick the category that matches the problem: bug, false positive, missed slop, mis-tagged, wrong fix, new rule, rule improvement or tool improvement. A tool improvement changes the tool or its docs, not one rule. Defects go to bug; rule changes go to rule improvement.
2. For a defect, pipe a minimal synthetic sample through `slopvac lint --stdin --format json`. For a proposal, write the current behavior, the proposed behavior and the reason instead. Never lint the user's own file for a report.
3. Run `slopvac report <category> --title ... --field ... --body-file <file> --gh`. It prints the exact title and body, writes the body to the file, prints the exact `gh issue create` command and files nothing.
4. Read the stderr warnings. Each names a field that may hold a credential or private data. Remove that text and rerun. The scrub is best effort; your reading of the preview still counts.
5. Send the preview and the command to the user and wait. Only approval of that exact text counts.
6. After approval, run the same command with `--yes`. It checks `gh` and its login, then runs `gh issue create` for you. Without `gh`, give the user the printed command or the prefilled form URL.

- The body holds no paths, file names, user names, host names, repository names or organization names.
- Put sample text inline. Add `--include-text <file>` only when the user agrees.
- Record the agent product, the model and the harness version as the harness reports them, or write N/A. Never read them from environment variables.
- Slopvac never reads a token. `gh` holds the login.
- An AI agent must say that an agent wrote the report.
